{"id":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line","title":"lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line","path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.md","line":3316,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex#lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line","uses":["[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement]]","[[references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement-involution]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2.tex","label":"lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line","line":5769,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[A Hyperplane is the Complement of its Normal Line]\n\\label{lem:hyperplane-eq-complement-normal-line}\n\n\\uses{lem:orthogonal-complement, lem:orthogonal-complement-involution}\n\n\n\n\nIf $W\\subseteq V$ is a hyperplane and $0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp$, then $\\operatorname{span}(x)^\\perp=W$.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n\\uses{lem:orthogonal-complement,lem:orthogonal-complement-involution}\n\\sketch Lemma \\ref{lem:orthogonal-complement} makes $W^\\perp$ one-dimensional, hence equal to $\\operatorname{span}(x)$; apply Lemma \\ref{lem:orthogonal-complement-involution}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[A Hyperplane is the Complement of its Normal Line] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6879706572706c616e652d65712d636f6d706c656d656e742d6e6f726d616c2d6c696e65\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement\">↗ lem:orthogonal-complement</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement-involution\">↗ lem:orthogonal-complement-involution</a> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W\\subseteq V$\">$W\\subseteq V$</span> is a hyperplane and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp $\">$0\\ne x\\in W^\\perp $</span>, then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {span}(x)^\\perp =W$\">$\\operatorname {span}(x)^\\perp =W$</span>.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement\">↗ lem:orthogonal-complement</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement-involution\">↗ lem:orthogonal-complement-involution</a> \\sketch Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6f7274686f676f6e616c2d636f6d706c656d656e74\">3</a> makes <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$W^\\perp $\">$W^\\perp $</span> one-dimensional, hence equal to <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\operatorname {span}(x)$\">$\\operatorname {span}(x)$</span>; apply Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FLeeRiemannian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2Fchapter2%23lem%3Aorthogonal-complement-involution\" data-tex-node=\"references/LeeRiemannian/blueprint/src/chapters/chapter2#lem:orthogonal-complement-involution\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6f7274686f676f6e616c2d636f6d706c656d656e742d696e766f6c7574696f6e\">3</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","